    fix(blocks): a step chains a channel's set only with the steps it would stack against, so a jog-room step no longer clamps a gap's steps onto one track (b12a2b-base item 7, lateral e3)
    
    In a block layout `ortho::place_tracks` splits a channel's steps into
    the sets whose plain rooms chain (`split_by_room`, item 1): the steps in
    a frame's jog room under its title strip and the steps in the gap
    outside the frame lie apart. The rooms were chained through any step,
    also one whose span meets neither set: a step beside the frame, its room
    reaching down past the frame's wall, chained the jog room to the gap.
    Placed as one stack, a displaced title-row end's step in the jog room
    then sat among the gap's steps in their turn order, every gap step on
    its far side was clamped to its room's end, and two long runs (the
    displaced exit's run on along the gap and another block's link to a
    frame further up) lay on one track; the router threw the first away and
    took it out through the frame's lateral wall (the case the lateral study
    calls e3, drawn BT). Two steps now chain only where they would stack:
    their spans meet within a track's pitch (as a channel's do) and their
    rooms within the least pitch. Outside a block layout nothing changes.
    
    Measured against 7122a53 (three checks): local judge A2 87 -> 86
    must-fail lines (one `lateral_x` line gone; two cells better inside
    failing lines: `lbl_crowd`, `lbl_endpx_mean`), A1 0, no cell worse;
    routed cells unchanged; suite-on failing tests 14 -> 14, no gate message
    new or worse. No repository fixture's drawing changes: the 332 + 32
    direction copies are identical to item 4a's, static and routed (the
    one copy the check marks, blocks/swimlane-nested TD `min_edge_gap`
    40 -> 25, is item 3's and is reported to the lead). Only seven local
    acceptance drawings change.
    
    Block mode only (behind the switch); default build byte-identical. New
    unit test ortho::tests::a_jog_room_step_does_not_chain_a_gaps_steps_onto_one_track
    (fails with the old chaining: two gap steps on one track). No snapshot
    or gate changes.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JGDFJkgB3ttBJtcTtc6aL5

